## 🔧 Microservices Deep Dive

### 1. Gateway Service (Port 3000)

**Purpose**: API Gateway, authentication, request routing, service health monitoring

**Tech Stack**:
- Express.js + TypeScript
- JWT authentication (jsonwebtoken)
- Redis for rate limiting
- Argon2 for password hashing
- Axios for service proxying

**Key Features**:
- ✅ User registration & login
- ✅ JWT token generation & validation
- ✅ Service registry with health checks
- ✅ Request proxying to microservices
- ✅ CORS & security middleware (Helmet)
- ⚠️ Rate limiting (commented out, ready to enable)

**Routes**:
```
POST   /api/auth/register
POST   /api/auth/login
POST   /api/auth/refresh
GET    /api/gateway/*           → AI Brain Service
GET    /api/gateway/lifestyle/* → Lifestyle Service
GET    /api/scheduler/*         → Scheduler Service
```

**Dependencies**:
```json
{
  "express": "^4.21.2",
  "jsonwebtoken": "^9.0.2",
  "argon2": "^0.44.0",
  "axios": "^1.7.9",
  "ioredis": "^5.4.2",
  "helmet": "^8.0.0",
  "zod": "^4.1.13"
}
```

**Key Files**:
- [src/server.ts](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/gateway-service/src/server.ts) - Main entry point
- [src/routes/auth.routes.ts](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/gateway-service/src/routes/auth.routes.ts) - Authentication endpoints
- `src/services/service-registry.service.ts` - Service health monitoring
- `src/middleware/error-handler.middleware.js` - Global error handling

---

### 2. Scheduler Service (Port 3001)

**Purpose**: Task management, calendar events, scheduling optimization

**Tech Stack**:
- Express.js + TypeScript
- Prisma ORM (PostgreSQL)
- RabbitMQ for async messaging
- date-fns for date manipulation

**Key Features**:
- ✅ Task CRUD with Eisenhower Matrix prioritization
- ✅ Category management
- ✅ Calendar events with conflict detection
- ✅ Reminder scheduling (15-min intervals)
- ✅ RabbitMQ event publishing
- ✅ Soft delete support

**Database Schema** (Prisma):
```prisma
model User {
  id         String   @id @default(uuid())
  email      String   @unique
  password   String
  name       String
  tasks      Task[]
  categories Category[]
  events     Event[]
}

model Task {
  id          String   @id @default(uuid())
  title       String
  description String?
  priority    String   // VI, VNI, NVI, NVNI (Eisenhower)
  status      String   // pending, in_progress, completed
  dueDate     DateTime?
  categoryId  String?
  userId      String
}

model Event {
  id          String   @id @default(uuid())
  title       String
  startTime   DateTime
  endTime     DateTime
  description String?
  userId      String
}
```

**Routes**:
```
GET    /api/tasks              - List tasks with filters
POST   /api/tasks              - Create task
PUT    /api/tasks/:id          - Update task
DELETE /api/tasks/:id          - Soft delete task
GET    /api/categories         - List categories
POST   /api/categories         - Create category
GET    /api/events             - List events
POST   /api/events             - Create event
```

**RabbitMQ Integration**:
- Publishes events: `task.created`, `task.updated`, `event.created`
- Exchanges: `scheduler.events`
- Queues: `task-events`, `event-events`

**Dependencies**:
```json
{
  "@prisma/client": "^7.0.0",
  "express": "^4.21.2",
  "amqplib": "^0.10.9",
  "date-fns": "^4.1.0",
  "zod": "^4.1.13"
}
```

---

### 3. AI Brain Service (Port 8000)

**Purpose**: Voice AI, natural language understanding, vector memory, ML predictions

**Tech Stack**:
- FastAPI + Python 3.11+
- OpenAI Whisper (STT)
- Groq Llama 3.3 70B (LLM)
- OpenAI TTS
- pgvector for semantic search
- MongoDB for conversation history

**Key Features**:
- ✅ Speech-to-Text (Whisper API)
- ✅ Text-to-Speech (OpenAI TTS with 6 voices)
- ✅ Emotion-based TTS (alloy, echo, fable, onyx, nova, shimmer)
- ✅ Natural Language Understanding (Groq LLM)
- ✅ Vector memory with semantic search
- ✅ Conversation context management
- ✅ Intent recognition
- 🚧 Habit prediction engine
- 🚧 Smart scheduling ML

**API Endpoints**:
```
POST   /api/ai/voice/transcribe         - STT (audio → text)
POST   /api/ai/voice/synthesize          - TTS (text → audio)
POST   /api/ai/voice/synthesize-emotion  - Emotion-based TTS
GET    /api/ai/voice/voices              - List available voices
POST   /api/ai/chat                      - NLU chat
POST   /api/ai/conversation/start        - Start conversation
POST   /api/ai/memory/store              - Store vector memory
GET    /api/ai/memory/search             - Semantic search
```

**AI Models**:
```python
{
  "STT": "whisper-1 (OpenAI)",
  "LLM": "llama-3.3-70b-versatile (Groq)",
  "TTS": "tts-1 (OpenAI)",
  "Embeddings": "text-embedding-3-small (OpenAI)" # Currently at quota
}
```

**Database**:
- **PostgreSQL**: Vector embeddings (pgvector extension)
- **MongoDB**: Conversation history, user context
- **Redis**: Response caching

**Dependencies**:
```python
{
  "fastapi": "^0.115.0",
  "openai": "^1.57.4",
  "groq": "^0.12.0",
  "motor": "^3.6.0",  # Async MongoDB
  "asyncpg": "^0.30.0",  # PostgreSQL
  "redis": "^5.2.1",
  "pydantic": "^2.10.4"
}
```

**Key Files**:
- [src/main.py](file:///media/code-buddy/code/Projects/Speak-Sync/apps/ai-brain-service/src/main.py) - FastAPI app
- `src/api/routes/voice.py` - Voice endpoints
- `src/api/routes/chat.py` - Chat/NLU
- `src/services/vector_memory_service.py` - Semantic memory
- `src/ml/` - ML models (habit prediction, scheduling)

